  "text": " make it 100. That means your cost per sale is half. Let me show you why this matters. Example, two businesses both making $1 million. One at 80% margins and spends $200 on costs, the other at 90% gross margins and spends $100,000 on costs. Same revenue, but the 90% business has an extra $100,000 to reinvest in growth, or better yet, profit. This compounds over time. To put this in perspective, to take a business from 80% to 90% gross margins, through price increases alone, you'd have to double your prices to get the same efficiency. That's a big deal. I obsess over this. So if you don't...",
